# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Clean URLs
/modular-compliance    https://modularcompliance.com     301
/services              /pages/services.html              200
/about                 /pages/about.html                 200
/privacy               /pages/privacy.html               200

# Catch old Simvoly paths if any
/blog/*                https://ournewnormal.co.nz/:splat  301

# Repo and tooling paths stay in git for CI and the marketing-truth hook.
# They must not be served. 404 is listed first because that is the status
# we want. Pages skips unsupported 404 redirect lines, so each source has
# a 302 fallback to /404.html, which Pages does apply when the asset exists.
# functions/[[path]].ts returns 404 for the same paths.
